      "id": "b000001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 1,
      "raw": "# MVVM Example (Model → ViewModel → QML)\n",
      "level": 1,
      "title": "MVVM Example (Model → ViewModel → QML)"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000002",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 2,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 3,
      "raw": "This example is buildable and runnable, and demonstrates the MVVM flow used in this repo:\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000004",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 4,
      "end_line": 4,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000005",
      "kind": "list",
      "start_line": 5,
      "end_line": 8,
      "raw": "- **Model (C++)** holds state and emits signals.\n- **ViewModel (C++)** exposes model state to QML and provides commands.\n- **View (QML)** binds to ViewModel and triggers commands.\n- **QmlContextBinder + ViewModelRegistry (C++)** register ViewModels and hand them to QML by key.\n",
      "items": [
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "**Model (C++)** holds state and emits signals.",
          "checked": null
        },
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "**ViewModel (C++)** exposes model state to QML and provides commands.",
          "checked": null
        },
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "**View (QML)** binds to ViewModel and triggers commands.",
          "checked": null
        },
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "**QmlContextBinder + ViewModelRegistry (C++)** register ViewModels and hand them to QML by key.",
          "checked": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b000006",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 9,
      "end_line": 9,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000007",
      "kind": "quote",
      "start_line": 10,
      "end_line": 10,
      "raw": "> This folder is both a reference implementation and a runnable sample target.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000008",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 11,
      "end_line": 11,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 12,
      "end_line": 12,
      "raw": "The sample shell now opts into the new layout contract explicitly: the window remains full-bleed and the card content is placed from `layoutSafeAreaBounds` rather than relying on automatic scaffold insets.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000010",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 13,
