    {
      "id": "b000032",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 42,
      "end_line": 42,
      "raw": "### `backend/ExampleModel.h` / `backend/ExampleModel.cpp`\n",
      "level": 3,
      "title": "`backend/ExampleModel.h` / `backend/ExampleModel.cpp`"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000033",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 43,
      "end_line": 43,
      "raw": "A minimal QObject model with a single property:\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000034",
      "kind": "list",
      "start_line": 44,
      "end_line": 44,
      "raw": "- `status` (QString)\n",
      "items": [
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "`status` (QString)",
          "checked": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b000035",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 45,
      "end_line": 45,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000036",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 46,
      "end_line": 46,
      "raw": "It emits `statusChanged()` when the value updates.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000037",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 47,
      "end_line": 47,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000038",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 48,
      "end_line": 48,
      "raw": "### `backend/ExampleViewModel.h` / `backend/ExampleViewModel.cpp`\n",
      "level": 3,
      "title": "`backend/ExampleViewModel.h` / `backend/ExampleViewModel.cpp`"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000039",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 49,
      "end_line": 49,
      "raw": "Wraps the model and exposes:\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000040",
      "kind": "list",
      "start_line": 50,
      "end_line": 51,
      "raw": "- `status` (READ-only from the model)\n- `simulateWork()` (optional command example; view-level writes can also be used)\n",
      "items": [
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "`status` (READ-only from the model)",
          "checked": null
        },
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "`simulateWork()` (optional command example; view-level writes can also be used)",
          "checked": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b000041",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 52,
      "end_line": 52,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000042",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 53,
      "end_line": 53,
      "raw": "It forwards `statusChanged()` to QML.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000043",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 54,
      "end_line": 54,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000044",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 55,
      "end_line": 55,
      "raw": "### `backend/ExampleBootstrap.h` / `backend/ExampleBootstrap.cpp`\n",
      "level": 3,
      "title": "`backend/ExampleBootstrap.h` / `backend/ExampleBootstrap.cpp`"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000045",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 56,
      "end_line": 56,
      "raw": "Builds a C++ ViewModel and registers it through `QmlContextBinder`:\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000046",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 57,
      "end_line": 57,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000047",
      "kind": "list",
      "start_line": 58,
      "end_line": 62,
      "raw": "- Constructs `ExampleModel` and `ExampleViewModel`\n- Declares a `QmlViewModelBinding`\n- Stores the ViewModel by key: `\"Example\"`\n- Claims writable ownership for view id `\"ExampleView\"`\n- Optionally exposes the same object as the `exampleViewModel` context property\n",
      "items": [
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "Constructs `ExampleModel` and `ExampleViewModel`",
          "checked": null
        },
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "Declares a `QmlViewModelBinding`",
          "checked": null
        },
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "Stores the ViewModel by key: `\"Example\"`",
          "checked": null
        },
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "Claims writable ownership for view id `\"ExampleView\"`",
          "checked": null
        },
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "Optionally exposes the same object as the `exampleViewModel` context property",
          "checked": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b000048",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 63,
      "end_line": 63,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000049",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 64,
      "end_line": 64,
      "raw": "### `qml/Main.qml`\n",
      "level": 3,
      "title": "`qml/Main.qml`"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000050",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 65,
      "end_line": 65,
      "raw": "Binds UI to the registered ViewModel:\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000051",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 66,
      "end_line": 66,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000052",
      "kind": "list",
      "start_line": 67,
      "end_line": 70,
      "raw": "- Uses the C++-declared view id: `\"ExampleView\"`\n- Fetches by view key: `LV.ViewModels.getForView(\"ExampleView\")`\n- Reads `vm.status`\n- Updates model through permission check: `LV.ViewModels.updateProperty(\"ExampleView\", \"status\", \"Working\")`\n",
      "items": [
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "Uses the C++-declared view id: `\"ExampleView\"`",
          "checked": null
        },
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "Fetches by view key: `LV.ViewModels.getForView(\"ExampleView\")`",
          "checked": null
        },
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "Reads `vm.status`",
          "checked": null
        },
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "Updates model through permission check: `LV.ViewModels.updateProperty(\"ExampleView\", \"status\", \"Working\")`",
          "checked": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b000053",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 71,
      "end_line": 71,
