    {
      "id": "b000056",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 74,
      "end_line": 74,
      "raw": "## Why a Registry?\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "Why a Registry?"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000057",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 75,
      "end_line": 75,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000058",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 76,
      "end_line": 77,
      "raw": "In MVVM, QML should not construct C++ models directly. Instead, the app bootstraps the ViewModels once\nand the UI simply **requests them by key**.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000059",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 78,
      "end_line": 78,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000060",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 79,
      "end_line": 79,
      "raw": "`ViewModels` is the bridge that keeps the View layer clean and declarative:\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000061",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 80,
      "end_line": 80,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000062",
      "kind": "list",
      "start_line": 81,
      "end_line": 82,
      "raw": "- **C++** controls lifetime and wiring\n- **QML** only consumes\n",
      "items": [
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "**C++** controls lifetime and wiring",
          "checked": null
        },
        {
          "marker": "-",
          "text": "**QML** only consumes",
          "checked": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b000063",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 83,
      "end_line": 83,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000064",
      "kind": "thematic_break",
      "start_line": 84,
      "end_line": 84,
      "raw": "---\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000065",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 85,
      "end_line": 85,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
